<title>POLAND: Zloty fixed weaker at 0.94 pct below parity rate.</title>
<headline>Zloty fixed weaker at 0.94 pct below parity rate.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Bank of Poland fixed the zloty at 3.5050 to the dollar, down from 3.4855 on Tuesday and at 1.8565 to the mark, down from 1.8555, the NBP said.</p>
<p>The central bank fixed the zloty at an average of 0.94 percent below the weighted dollar and mark parity rates, weaker than Tuesday's fix at -0.67 percent.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
